   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Simulated Cursor\n\nA synthetic mouse cursor that travels between waypoints and fires a click ripple, for narrating a UI on screen.\n\nCategory: effects. Length: 5 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- You are narrating a screen demo and need a synthetic cursor that moves predictably over a UI screenshot or recording.\n- You want to direct attention to a specific element by having the cursor travel to it and click.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You need a real screen recording: this draws a synthetic overlay, not a capture.\n- The video is abstract or non-UI: a floating arrow reads as a tutorial and breaks the mood.\n- The underlying layout shifts between scenes: waypoints are absolute reference pixels.\n\nVariables:\n- points (string): Waypoints, default \"[{\\\"x\\\":200,\\\"y\\\":150,\\\"hold\\\":20},{\\\"x\\\":800,\\\"y\\\":360,\\\"hold\\\":25,\\\"click\\\":true},{\\\"x\\\":1050,\\\"y\\\":560,\\\"hold\\\":20}]\"\n- frame_width (number, 200-4000): Frame width, default 1280\n- frame_height (number, 200-4000): Frame height, default 720\n- color (color): Color, default \"#ffffff\"\n- size (number, 12-96): Size, default 32\n- speed (number, 0.25-3): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Simulated Cursor\n\n  A synthetic mouse cursor that travels between waypoints and fires a click ripple, for narrating a UI on screen.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/simulated-cursor/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"simulated-cursor\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"5\"\n  data-composition-variables='[{\"id\":\"points\",\"type\":\"string\",\"role\":\"content\",\"label\":\"Waypoints\",\"description\":\"JSON array of {x, y, hold, click} in the reference frame (1280×720 by default): x and y are where the cursor rests, hold is frames to rest there, click fires a ripple on arrival.\",\"default\":\"[{\\\"x\\\":200,\\\"y\\\":150,\\\"hold\\\":20},{\\\"x\\\":800,\\\"y\\\":360,\\\"hold\\\":25,\\\"click\\\":true},{\\\"x\\\":1050,\\\"y\\\":560,\\\"hold\\\":20}]\"},{\"id\":\"frame_width\",\"type\":\"number\",\"role\":\"layout\",\"label\":\"Frame width\",\"description\":\"Width of the reference frame the waypoints live in; it is scaled to fit.\",\"default\":1280,\"min\":200,\"max\":4000,\"step\":1,\"unit\":\"px\"},{\"id\":\"frame_height\",\"type\":\"number\",\"role\":\"layout\",\"label\":\"Frame height\",\"description\":\"Height of the reference frame the waypoints live in.\",\"default\":720,\"min\":200,\"max\":4000,\"step\":1,\"unit\":\"px\"},{\"id\":\"color\",\"type\":\"color\",\"role\":\"style\",\"label\":\"Color\",\"description\":\"Cursor fill color.\",\"default\":\"#ffffff\"},{\"id\":\"size\",\"type\":\"number\",\"role\":\"style\",\"label\":\"Size\",\"description\":\"Cursor size in reference pixels.\",\"default\":32,\"min\":12,\"max\":96,\"step\":1,\"unit\":\"px\"},{\"id\":\"speed\",\"type\":\"number\",\"role\":\"motion\",\"label\":\"Speed\",\"description\":\"Playback speed multiplier.\",\"default\":1,\"min\":0.25,\"max\":3,\"step\":0.05,\"unit\":\"x\"}]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Simulated Cursor</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n\n        }\n        .scu-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; }\n        .scu-field { overflow: visible; }\n        .scu-cursor { position: absolute; transform-origin: top left; }\n        .scu-cursor svg { display: block; }\n        .scu-ripple { position: absolute; width: 160px; height: 160px; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"simulated-cursor\" data-duration=\"5\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"scu-clip\" class=\"scu-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"5\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div id=\"scu-field\" class=\"scu-field\">\n            <svg id=\"scu-ripple\" class=\"scu-ripple\" viewBox=\"0 0 160 160\"><circle id=\"scu-ring\" cx=\"80\" cy=\"80\" r=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\" opacity=\"0\"></circle></svg>\n            <div id=\"scu-cursor\" class=\"scu-cursor\">\n              <svg id=\"scu-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M5 3L5 19L9.5 14.5L12.5 21L15 20L12 13.5L18.5 13.5L5 3Z\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" id=\"scu-path\"></path></svg>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"boolean\" ? value : value === \"true\" ? true : value === \"false\" ? false : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, options, fallback) {\n              return options.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            // Frame-based helpers, written from their definitions.\n            var Easing = (function () {\n              function bezier(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n                return function (x) {\n                  if (x <= 0) return 0;\n                  if (x >= 1) return 1;\n                  var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n                  for (var i = 0; i < 40; i++) {\n                    var u = 1 - t;\n                    var cx = 3 * u * u * t * x1 + 3 * u * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n                    if (Math.abs(cx - x) < 1e-6) break;\n                    if (cx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n                    t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                  }\n                  var v = 1 - t;\n                  return 3 * v * v * t * y1 + 3 * v * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n                };\n              }\n              return {\n                bezier: bezier,\n                linear: function (t) { return t; },\n                quad: function (t) { return t * t; },\n                cubic: function (t) { return t * t * t; },\n                sin: function (t) { return 1 - Math.cos((t * Math.PI) / 2); },\n                poly: function (n) { return function (t) { return Math.pow(t, n); }; },\n                ease: bezier(0.42, 0, 1, 1),\n                out: function (f) { return function (t) { return 1 - f(1 - t); }; },\n                inOut: function (f) { return function (t) { return t < 0.5 ? f(t * 2) / 2 : 1 - f((1 - t) * 2) / 2; }; }\n              };\n            })();\n            function interpolate(input, inR, outR, o) {\n              o = o || {};\n              var n = inR.length;\n              var left = o.extrapolateLeft || \"extend\";\n              var right = o.extrapolateRight || \"extend\";\n              var i = 1;\n              while (i < n - 1 && input > inR[i]) i++;\n              var a = inR[i - 1], b = inR[i];\n              if (input < inR[0] && left === \"clamp\") return outR[0];\n              if (input > inR[n - 1] && right === \"clamp\") return outR[n - 1];\n              var t = b === a ? 0 : (input - a) / (b - a);\n              if (o.easing) t = o.easing(t);\n              return outR[i - 1] + (outR[i] - outR[i - 1]) * t;\n            }\n            // Damped spring from rest to 1. durationInFrames stretches time so the spring has settled by then.\n            function spring(o) {\n              var c = o.config || {};\n              var mass = c.mass != null ? c.mass : 1;\n              var k = c.stiffness != null ? c.stiffness : 100;\n              var damp = c.damping != null ? c.damping : 10;\n              function at(t) {\n                var w0 = Math.sqrt(k / mass);\n                var z = damp / (2 * Math.sqrt(k * mass));\n                if (z < 1) {\n                  var wd = w0 * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z);\n                  return 1 - Math.exp(-z * w0 * t) * (Math.cos(wd * t) + ((z * w0) / wd) * Math.sin(wd * t));\n                }\n                return 1 - Math.exp(-w0 * t) * (1 + w0 * t);\n              }\n              var t = Math.max(0, o.frame) / o.fps;\n              if (o.durationInFrames) {\n                var settle = 4, step = 1 / o.fps;\n                for (var s = settle; s > 0.05; s -= step) {\n                  if (Math.abs(1 - at(s)) > 0.001) { settle = s + step; break; }\n                  settle = s;\n                }\n                t = (Math.max(0, o.frame) / o.durationInFrames) * settle;\n                if (o.frame >= o.durationInFrames) return 1;\n              }\n              return at(t);\n            }\n            function parseColor(c) {\n              var m;\n              c = String(c).trim();\n              if ((m = /^#([0-9a-f]{3,8})$/i.exec(c))) {\n                var h = m[1];\n                if (h.length <= 4) h = h.split(\"\").map(function (x) { return x + x; }).join(\"\");\n                return [parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16), parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16), parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16), h.length === 8 ? parseInt(h.slice(6, 8), 16) / 255 : 1];\n              }\n              if ((m = /^rgba?\\(([^)]+)\\)/i.exec(c))) {\n                var p = m[1].split(\",\").map(Number);\n                return [p[0], p[1], p[2], p.length > 3 ? p[3] : 1];\n              }\n              return [0, 0, 0, 1];\n            }\n            function interpolateColors(t, inR, outR) {\n              var a = parseColor(outR[0]), b = parseColor(outR[1]);\n              var u = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (t - inR[0]) / (inR[1] - inR[0])));\n              return \"rgba(\" + [0, 1, 2].map(function (i) { return Math.round(a[i] + (b[i] - a[i]) * u); }).join(\",\") + \",\" + (a[3] + (b[3] - a[3]) * u) + \")\";\n            }\n            // Seeded 0..1 value: the same seed always gives the same number.\n            function random(seed) {\n              var s = String(seed), h = 2166136261;\n              for (var i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\n                h ^= s.charCodeAt(i);\n                h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);\n              }\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 13), 2246822519);\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 16), 3266489917);\n              return ((h ^ (h >>> 15)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n            }\n            // Fit a fixed-size design stage into the frame.\n            function fit(el, w, h, fill) {\n              var s = Math.min(root.clientWidth / w, root.clientHeight / h) * (fill || 1);\n              el.style.position = \"absolute\";\n              el.style.left = \"50%\";\n              el.style.top = \"50%\";\n              el.style.width = w + \"px\";\n              el.style.height = h + \"px\";\n              el.style.transform = \"translate(-50%, -50%) scale(\" + s + \")\";\n              return s;\n            }\n            // Drive draw(frame) from the timeline so seeking always draws the same picture.\n            function clockTween(tl, totalFrames, draw, rate) {\n              var clock = { frame: 0 };\n              tl.to(clock, { frame: totalFrames, duration: totalFrames / 30, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(clock.frame * (rate || 1)); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n            }\n            var SVGNS = \"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\";\n            function svgEl(tag, attrs, parent) {\n              var e = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, tag);\n              for (var k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]);\n              if (parent) parent.appendChild(e);\n              return e;\n            }\n\n\n            var color = str(vars.color, \"#ffffff\");\n            var size = num(vars.size, 32, 12, 96);\n            var speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0.25, 3);\n            var points = [{ x: 200, y: 150, hold: 20 }, { x: 800, y: 360, hold: 25, click: true }, { x: 1050, y: 560, hold: 20 }];\n            try {\n              var parsed = JSON.parse(str(vars.points, \"\"));\n              if (Array.isArray(parsed) && parsed.length > 0) points = parsed.map(function (p) { return { x: Number(p.x) || 0, y: Number(p.y) || 0, hold: p.hold == null ? undefined : Number(p.hold), click: !!p.click }; });\n            } catch (e) {}\n            var field = document.getElementById(\"scu-field\");\n            fit(field, num(vars.frame_width, 1280, 200, 4000), num(vars.frame_height, 720, 200, 4000), 1);\n            var cursorEl = document.getElementById(\"scu-cursor\");\n            var cursorSvg = document.getElementById(\"scu-svg\");\n            var rippleSvg = document.getElementById(\"scu-ripple\");\n            var ring = document.getElementById(\"scu-ring\");\n            document.getElementById(\"scu-path\").setAttribute(\"fill\", color);\n            ring.setAttribute(\"stroke\", color);\n            cursorSvg.setAttribute(\"width\", size);\n            cursorSvg.setAttribute(\"height\", size);\n            cursorEl.style.width = size + \"px\";\n            cursorEl.style.height = size + \"px\";\n\n            // Rest at the first point for its hold, then 24 frames of travel per leg, then each point's hold.\n            var segments = [], cursor = points[0].hold == null ? 0 : points[0].hold;\n            for (var i = 0; i < points.length - 1; i++) {\n              var to = points[i + 1];\n              var start = cursor, end = start + 24;\n              var holdEnd = end + (to.hold == null ? 15 : to.hold);\n              segments.push({ start: start, end: end, holdEnd: holdEnd, from: points[i], to: to });\n              cursor = holdEnd;\n            }\n            function draw(frame) {\n              var x = points[0].x, y = points[0].y, clickFrame = null;\n              for (var s = 0; s < segments.length; s++) {\n                var seg = segments[s];\n                if (frame >= seg.start && frame < seg.holdEnd) {\n                  if (frame < seg.end) {\n                    x = interpolate(frame, [seg.start, seg.end], [seg.from.x, seg.to.x], { extrapolateLeft: \"clamp\", extrapolateRight: \"clamp\" });\n                    y = interpolate(frame, [seg.start, seg.end], [seg.from.y, seg.to.y], { extrapolateLeft: \"clamp\", extrapolateRight: \"clamp\" });\n                  } else {\n                    x = seg.to.x; y = seg.to.y;\n                    if (seg.to.click) clickFrame = frame - seg.end;\n                  }\n                  break;\n                }\n                if (frame >= seg.holdEnd) { x = seg.to.x; y = seg.to.y; }\n              }\n              var scale = 1, radius = 0, opacity = 0;\n              if (clickFrame !== null) {\n                var dip = spring({ fps: 30, frame: clickFrame, config: { damping: 10, stiffness: 200, mass: 0.6 }, durationInFrames: 14 });\n                scale = 1 - dip * 0.18;\n                radius = interpolate(clickFrame, [0, 24], [4, 60], { extrapolateLeft: \"clamp\", extrapolateRight: \"clamp\" });\n                opacity = interpolate(clickFrame, [0, 24], [0.6, 0], { extrapolateLeft: \"clamp\", extrapolateRight: \"clamp\" });\n              }\n              ring.setAttribute(\"r\", radius);\n              ring.setAttribute(\"opacity\", opacity);\n              rippleSvg.style.left = x - 80 + \"px\";\n              rippleSvg.style.top = y - 80 + \"px\";\n              rippleSvg.style.display = opacity > 0 ? \"block\" : \"none\";\n              cursorEl.style.left = x + \"px\";\n              cursorEl.style.top = y + \"px\";\n              cursorEl.style.transform = \"scale(\" + scale + \")\";\n            }\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            clockTween(tl, 150, draw, speed);\n\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"5\");\n            if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"simulated-cursor\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
